From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:59:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] check this setup: the sentence of the player information with
 the frames lost in steady playback

Kodi's player information now says frames that it lost only where the
loss is sustained in steady playback, and by its cause: how many were
dropped by the player (frames_dropped) or came too late for the
display (frames_skipped), the graphics busy with the percent they are
in use (frames_gpu), or a note that the stream was buffering
(frames_buffering). Check this setup reads that sentence of the clip
it plays and says it in its own words (picture_lines()): it did not
know the four codes, and said "everything as intended" for them.

They now have their strings of Estuary in SUM, the number before the
sentence for frames_dropped and frames_skipped (as frames_failed), and
the percent after it for frames_gpu.

Host test (stand-ins for Kodi, tools/regress kodi-host ux:
check_verdict_test.py, with Estuary's Variables.xml of the Kodi tree):
every code of the sentence has the same string as in Estuary, and the
four are said, never as "everything as intended". It fails without
this change and passes with it.
---
 resources/lib/hades_check.py | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/resources/lib/hades_check.py b/resources/lib/hades_check.py
index 4e1cbdc..44379f0 100644
--- a/resources/lib/hades_check.py
+++ b/resources/lib/hades_check.py
@@ -395,7 +395,8 @@ HEAD = {'dv': 52700, 'dv_hdr10': 52701, 'dv_sdr': 52702, 'hdr10plus': 52703, 'hd
         'hlg': 52705, 'sdr': 52706, 'hdr_lost': 52707, 'hdr_as_sdr': 52595}
 SUM = {'ok': 52710, 'dv_not_native': 52711, 'hdr_to_sdr': 52712, 'hdr_not_sent': 52713,
        'frames_failed': 52714, 'step_down': 52715, 'fel_resync': 52716, 'rate_mismatch': 52717,
-       'audio_decoded': 52718, 'unknown_output': 52719, 'hdr_as_sdr': 52596}
+       'audio_decoded': 52718, 'unknown_output': 52719, 'hdr_as_sdr': 52596,
+       'frames_dropped': 52752, 'frames_skipped': 52753, 'frames_gpu': 52755, 'frames_buffering': 52757}
 HDR_WHY = {'noprop': 52720, 'noedid': 52721, 'nostatic': 52722, 'noeotf': 52723, 'noblob': 52724,
            'notqueued': 52724, 'setting': 52725}
 AUDIO_WHY = {'syncdisplay': 52726, 'passthroughoff': 52727, 'codecoff': 52728}
@@ -517,8 +518,10 @@ def picture_lines(fmt, info, answer, dark=None, light=None, shown=True):
     elif code == 'audio_decoded':
         # (a clip of the check has no sound: not said)
         verdict = [('e', SUM['ok'])]
-    elif code == 'frames_failed':
+    elif code in ('frames_failed', 'frames_dropped', 'frames_skipped'):
         verdict = [('t', arg + ' '), ('e', SUM[code])]
+    elif code == 'frames_gpu':
+        verdict = [('e', SUM[code]), ('t', ' ' + arg + ' %.')]
     elif code in SUM:
         verdict = [('e', SUM[code])]
     elif head:
